    "tfm_sensitive": false,
    "summary": "Concrete ViewDataDictionary iteration is forced through interface-returning enumerators.",
    "explanation": "ViewDataDictionary exposes only explicit IEnumerable<T> and IEnumerable GetEnumerator implementations. Concrete foreach therefore cannot bind to a public pattern-based enumerator, and returning the underlying dictionary enumerator as IEnumerator<T> can box its struct enumerator on the per-request view-data path.",
    "snippet": "IEnumerator<KeyValuePair<string, object?>> IEnumerable<KeyValuePair<string, object?>>.GetEnumerator()\n{\n    return _data.GetEnumerator();\n}\n\nIEnumerator IEnumerable.GetEnumerator()\n{\n    return _data.GetEnumerator();\n}",
    "suppressed": false
  },
